WEBVTT

00:00.950 --> 00:02.060
<i>Huh?</i>

00:02.060 --> 00:04.440
<i>Is </i>A Tale of Perishing<i>...</i>

00:04.440 --> 00:06.510
<i>supposed to be this happy?</i>

00:09.480 --> 00:10.900
Well, whatever.

00:12.410 --> 00:13.990
Of course it's not.

00:14.730 --> 00:16.540
<i>This weird bird...</i>

00:17.700 --> 00:21.800
Man, I ate way too much.
My diet starts tomorrow.

00:21.800 --> 00:22.830
It's no use.

00:24.540 --> 00:26.030
<i>No matter where I go...</i>

00:27.380 --> 00:28.560
It's no use.

00:28.560 --> 00:30.040
<i>No matter what I do...</i>

00:30.220 --> 00:31.540
It's no use.

00:31.540 --> 00:33.540
<i>This bird just keeps showing up.</i>

00:33.540 --> 00:34.790
It's no use.

00:34.980 --> 00:36.040
It's no use.

00:36.220 --> 00:37.810
It's no use.

00:42.000 --> 00:43.260
It's no use.

00:43.430 --> 00:45.780
It's no use. It's no use.

00:45.780 --> 00:49.630
That overgrown chicken 
<i>seriously</i> pisses me off.

02:20.070 --> 02:23.990
Episode 8: CONFESSION

02:26.670 --> 02:30.880
Still, I'm almost certain I've seen 
that thing somewhere before.

02:30.880 --> 02:32.500
Natsuko!

02:33.240 --> 02:34.500
Find out something?

02:34.500 --> 02:38.910
That talking bird may be 
the same as you, Natsuko.

02:38.910 --> 02:39.620
Huh?

02:39.850 --> 02:44.540
Most of the town's residents are folks 
evacuated from the nine kingdoms.

02:44.540 --> 02:48.760
But that bird isn't from 
any of those kingdoms.

02:48.760 --> 02:53.550
So perhaps it came from the 
Kingdom of Reality, just like you.

02:54.770 --> 02:58.800
Also, there are two places 
where this bird frequently shows up.

02:58.800 --> 03:00.900
The first is around you, Natsuko.

03:01.120 --> 03:02.400
The other is...

03:06.760 --> 03:09.250
My, what an adorable little bird.

03:10.610 --> 03:12.170
Would you like a flower?

03:21.500 --> 03:24.180
Nacchan! I caught it!

03:26.190 --> 03:29.440
You can try to get away, but, "It's no use."

03:33.980 --> 03:36.070
So who are you? Where'd you come from?

03:36.070 --> 03:37.420
What's your goal?

03:37.420 --> 03:38.920
It's no use asking me.

03:38.920 --> 03:40.860
Oh, I see. Justice!

03:40.860 --> 03:43.790
Right-o. Ready when you are.

03:44.080 --> 03:48.480
Destiny, go tell the kids they're
getting a whole roast chicken today.

03:48.480 --> 03:50.450
Wow, I'm so excited!

03:50.450 --> 03:52.570
Master, whatcha doin'?

03:53.160 --> 03:55.120
I wanna cook, too.

03:55.120 --> 03:56.040
Me, too.

03:56.250 --> 03:58.200
It's dangerous here, so go over there.

03:58.200 --> 03:59.290
Aw.

03:59.290 --> 04:01.440
But we wanna play!

04:00.600 --> 04:03.660
It seems "Master" Justice is quite popular.

04:03.660 --> 04:04.950
Sh-Shut up!

04:04.950 --> 04:06.800
I gotta pee.

04:06.090 --> 04:06.800
Huh?

04:06.800 --> 04:11.160
Huh? W-Wait! No, don't go here! Wait, wait!

04:07.070 --> 04:07.870
Oh, my.

04:07.590 --> 04:10.180
I can't hold it.

04:08.490 --> 04:11.160
Juschan! This way! Hurry!

04:11.160 --> 04:12.610
"Juschan"?

04:13.690 --> 04:16.570
The <i>real</i> Destiny is a beautiful maiden.

04:16.800 --> 04:19.690
That pile of muscles is not Destiny.

04:19.690 --> 04:23.700
What? But the current Destiny 
that's all ripped is awesome.

04:24.390 --> 04:26.210
Hey! Give that back.

04:26.210 --> 04:27.870
<i>This</i> is Destiny.

04:27.870 --> 04:30.850
Uh, wait, this is...

04:31.130 --> 04:32.370
<b>Kametaro
Tsuruyama</b>

04:31.590 --> 04:32.380
Huh?

04:32.590 --> 04:34.690
Isn't this Director Tsuruyama's autograph?

04:38.060 --> 04:41.140
Are you Director Kametaro Tsuruyama?

04:41.140 --> 04:42.350
And what if I am?

04:42.570 --> 04:44.460
Wait, seriously? No way.

04:44.460 --> 04:47.080
Director? Director of what?

04:47.080 --> 04:51.020
She's the director that created <i>A Tale of 
Perishing</i>. A virtuoso of the anime world!

04:51.020 --> 04:54.200
I-I'm a huge fan! Please shake my hand!

04:55.070 --> 04:58.800
U-Um, I've seen all your works,
and got all your Blu-rays.

04:59.020 --> 05:02.750
O-Oh, could you write, 
"To Miss Natsuko Hirose," here?

05:03.330 --> 05:04.480
No "Miss" for you.

05:08.740 --> 05:11.660
Thank you so much.
This is now a family heirloom.

05:11.660 --> 05:15.410
Um, I looked up to you so much, I ended up 
at Studio Konkon since you worked there.

05:15.410 --> 05:18.670
Still, I never dreamed 
I'd get to meet you like this.

05:19.060 --> 05:19.920
But wait.

05:19.960 --> 05:21.380
<b>Kametaro Tsuruyama, renowned virtuoso of the anime industry, 
known for many works including the feature film, <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>, 
has died. Her relatives grew worried when they couldn't get hold
 of Director Tsuruyama, and went to check on her at home, 
where they found her unresponsive. The cause of death is 
thought to be food poisoning.</b>

05:20.980 --> 05:22.760
You died, didn't you?

05:21.380 --> 05:22.300
<b>Kametaro Tsuruyama, renowned virtuoso of the anime industry, 
known for many works including the feature film, <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>, 
has died. Her relatives grew worried when they couldn't get hold
 of Director Tsuruyama, and went to check on her at home, 
where they found her unresponsive. The cause of death is 
thought to be food poisoning.</b>

05:22.300 --> 05:22.680
<b>Kametaro Tsuruyama, renowned virtuoso of the anime industry, 
known for many works including the feature film, <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>, 
has died. Her relatives grew worried when they couldn't get hold
 of Director Tsuruyama, and went to check on her at home, 
where they found her unresponsive. The cause of death is 
thought to be food poisoning.</b>

05:22.680 --> 05:23.180
<b>Kametaro Tsuruyama, renowned virtuoso of the anime industry, 
known for many works including the feature film, <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>, 
has died. Her relatives grew worried when they couldn't get hold
 of Director Tsuruyama, and went to check on her at home, 
where they found her unresponsive. The cause of death is 
thought to be food poisoning.</b>

05:22.760 --> 05:24.680
I saw your obituary.

05:23.180 --> 05:23.550
<b>Kametaro Tsuruyama, renowned virtuoso of the anime industry, 
known for many works including the feature film, <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>, 
has died. Her relatives grew worried when they couldn't get hold
 of Director Tsuruyama, and went to check on her at home, 
where they found her unresponsive. The cause of death is 
thought to be food poisoning.</b>

05:23.550 --> 05:24.640
<b>Kametaro Tsuruyama, renowned virtuoso of the anime industry, 
known for many works including the feature film, <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>, 
has died. Her relatives grew worried when they couldn't get hold
 of Director Tsuruyama, and went to check on her at home, 
where they found her unresponsive. The cause of death is 
thought to be food poisoning.</b>

05:24.670 --> 05:29.810
Hm? I guess that means I died, too. 
So this really is that reincarnation thing.

05:29.810 --> 05:32.280
But wait, how'd you end up a bird?

05:32.280 --> 05:34.800
I died and gained wings.

05:34.800 --> 05:37.640
Huh? Is that how this works?

05:37.640 --> 05:39.560
What did you gain when you died?

05:39.560 --> 05:43.480
Huh? Wh-What did I gain? Oh, maybe this?

05:44.620 --> 05:48.370
Nope. This existed in reality.

05:48.370 --> 05:50.120
You haven't gained anything.

05:50.120 --> 05:52.980
I guess the Kingdom of Reality 
really does exist.

05:52.980 --> 05:55.220
This is the pegbar I was using.

05:55.220 --> 05:56.740
Huh? No way!

05:58.240 --> 06:00.540
H-Hey, what are you doing?

06:00.760 --> 06:05.040
Are you planning on using that pegbar's 
powers to revise <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>?

06:05.040 --> 06:05.610
Huh?

06:05.870 --> 06:10.880
Even if you try to revise... 
no, to <i>fix</i> all of my movie, it's no use.

06:10.880 --> 06:14.920
Me? Fix all of <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>?

06:15.520 --> 06:18.600
I-I'd never do something like that.

06:18.600 --> 06:21.080
<i>A Tale of Perishing</i> is my bible.

06:21.080 --> 06:24.180
I've been obsessed with it 
ever since I first saw it in the theater.

06:24.180 --> 06:26.130
It's where I got started.

06:26.640 --> 06:28.770
Then, why are you defeating the Voids?

06:28.770 --> 06:32.170
Huh? Well, I mean, they're attacking us...

06:32.560 --> 06:36.710
More importantly, could you 
stop timing everything I say?

06:36.710 --> 06:40.060
Ever since you showed up, 
the overall runtime just keeps growing.

06:40.060 --> 06:43.210
You have no idea how many scenes I've had 
to cut with tears streaming down my face.

06:43.210 --> 06:46.440
Huh? Like what? Tell me more 
about these scenes that got cut.

06:46.440 --> 06:49.090
It's no use. Just run off 
back to reality already.

06:49.090 --> 06:50.970
Huh? I can go back? How?

06:50.970 --> 06:52.840
How would I know? Figure it out yourself.

06:52.840 --> 06:54.180
Aw, c'mon.

06:54.180 --> 06:58.300
No matter how much you try to resist it, 
this film's ending is already set in stone.

06:59.110 --> 07:02.090
Luke's demise is already in motion.

07:02.090 --> 07:04.500
Try as you might, it's no use.

07:05.340 --> 07:07.480
Uh, h-hey!

07:07.480 --> 07:08.710
Wait!

07:10.540 --> 07:13.540
Natsuko, what did she mean 
by "Luke's demise"?

07:18.220 --> 07:19.870
Cheers!

07:23.240 --> 07:25.370
So what was it you wanted to talk about?

07:25.370 --> 07:27.380
Oh, well, uh...

07:27.680 --> 07:32.030
It's not actually about me. 
It's about a friend of a friend.

07:32.030 --> 07:34.610
Huh? A friend of a friend?

07:34.610 --> 07:35.390
Yeah.

07:35.390 --> 07:39.940
We've been together since we were born.
Do you <i>have</i> any other friends, Luke?

07:41.140 --> 07:42.160
Never mind.

07:42.160 --> 07:45.070
Ah, no, wait, I was just kidding.
Come on, let's talk.

07:45.070 --> 07:49.040
Is this friend of a friend 
in some kind of trouble?

07:49.040 --> 07:51.140
You can tell me anything.

07:51.660 --> 07:53.790
Well, this friend of a friend is...

07:54.250 --> 07:55.170
Yes?

07:57.510 --> 08:00.170
...apparently in love with someone.

08:01.410 --> 08:02.030
Huh?

08:02.370 --> 08:05.580
Um, they've never felt that way before,

08:05.580 --> 08:08.370
so they don't know what to do.

08:08.820 --> 08:11.310
They just can't concentrate on anything.

08:11.920 --> 08:13.820
How far have you gotten?

08:13.820 --> 08:15.210
What do you mean?

08:15.210 --> 08:16.630
Are you guys dating?

08:16.630 --> 08:18.950
Y-You idiot! No! It's not like that!

08:18.950 --> 08:20.840
Oh, thank goodness.

08:21.430 --> 08:22.840
I'm considering marriage.

08:24.850 --> 08:27.860
I just think these things
should be done properly.

08:28.280 --> 08:31.420
Uh, I mean, that's what 
my friend's <i>friend</i> is thinking.

08:31.420 --> 08:34.310
Nope, nope, nope, nope! <i>Absolutely</i> not!

08:34.310 --> 08:35.050
No?

08:35.050 --> 08:36.890
Well, of course not.

08:36.890 --> 08:39.330
I mean, the other person 
would find that creepy.

08:39.990 --> 08:42.880
You haven't even told them
how you feel, right?

08:42.880 --> 08:46.450
If you suddenly ask them to 
marry you, that'd be horrifying.

08:46.650 --> 08:48.880
How I feel?

08:48.880 --> 08:51.620
Aw, love trouble!

08:51.620 --> 08:53.740
Oh, to be young again!

08:52.910 --> 08:53.990
Feelings, huh?

08:53.990 --> 08:56.360
Luke? Hey, wait! H-Hey!

08:56.360 --> 08:58.440
And? What about you?

08:58.440 --> 09:01.480
You're having love trouble, too, right? 
You can tell me!

09:01.480 --> 09:03.560
Some bittersweet honey buns!

09:01.850 --> 09:05.810
W-Wait! H-Hey, Luke!

09:11.030 --> 09:14.700
The ending's already set in stone, huh?

09:15.830 --> 09:18.340
<i>Is all that really going 
to play out after this?</i>

09:19.190 --> 09:23.190
<i>In the movie, he falls deeper and deeper 
into despair because his friends die one by one.</i>

09:23.190 --> 09:24.940
<i>But Unio didn't die.</i>

09:25.340 --> 09:27.230
<i>And I don't see Destiny dying, either.</i>

09:29.010 --> 09:32.110
<i>I just can't see Luke 
ending up like that right now.</i>

09:32.110 --> 09:34.950
<i>But if it goes like the director said, 
that means in the end...</i>

09:37.250 --> 09:41.260
<i>Reality... Can I even go back? And how?</i>

09:41.260 --> 09:42.180
Natsuko!

09:43.350 --> 09:44.520
Luke?

09:50.540 --> 09:51.490
What is it?

09:57.020 --> 09:58.180
I love you!

10:07.350 --> 10:08.370
I...

10:09.270 --> 10:11.100
I love you.

10:16.010 --> 10:16.940
I love you.

10:20.940 --> 10:21.680
Huh?

10:22.890 --> 10:24.390
<b>To
Natsuko
Hirose</b>

10:22.890 --> 10:24.390
<b>Kametaro
Tsuruyama</b>

10:28.580 --> 10:30.820
<i>Uh, what? What's going on?</i>

10:31.450 --> 10:34.750
<i>Luke's an anime character 
I've been watching since I was a kid.</i>

10:34.750 --> 10:40.150
<i>But the Luke right in front of me is real.
 He makes me food, fights, and is alive.</i>

10:40.150 --> 10:44.920
<i>No, wait. I died, right? 
So maybe this isn't real?</i>

10:47.890 --> 10:51.190
<i>This is the world of the movie, 
</i>A Tale of Perishing<i>.</i>

10:53.550 --> 10:54.670
Natsuko.

10:54.920 --> 10:55.790
I love you.

10:56.780 --> 10:59.050
<i>Since I reincarnated, am I dead?</i>

11:03.180 --> 11:04.070
I love you.

11:04.310 --> 11:07.310
<i>Or am I alive? Is this real?</i>

11:07.670 --> 11:11.180
<i>If this </i>is<i> real, Luke's just a bunch 
of lines on animation paper.</i>

11:11.710 --> 11:16.070
<i>I remember reading Director Tsuruyama used 
3B pencils, so maybe he's drawn with 3B...</i>

11:16.070 --> 11:18.450
<i>No, this isn't the time 
to be thinking about that.</i>

11:18.720 --> 11:19.600
I love you!

11:20.700 --> 11:23.830
<i>These lines drawn with 
a 2B or 3B pencil keep saying:</i>

11:23.830 --> 11:24.820
I love you.

11:24.820 --> 11:27.190
<i>Um, s-so, uh...</i>

11:27.190 --> 11:28.240
I love you.

11:28.410 --> 11:29.460
I love you.

11:29.460 --> 11:30.620
I love you!

11:34.340 --> 11:38.090
I wonder if this is the demise of Luke
 the bird was talking about.

11:38.090 --> 11:39.850
It would certainly qualify.

11:42.630 --> 11:45.340
Stop.

11:46.810 --> 11:47.780
I love you.

11:49.250 --> 11:50.220
Oh, right.

11:50.850 --> 11:53.180
I have to head to the dubbing session.

11:53.180 --> 11:54.230
Natsuko?

11:54.230 --> 11:58.160
Brrring, brrring. Hello? Yes, this is Hirose.

11:58.160 --> 11:59.230
Wait, what's wrong?

11:59.230 --> 12:02.050
Yes, that's right. No more retakes.

12:02.050 --> 12:06.230
No more recap episodes. I don't want 
to think about anything anymore.

12:09.380 --> 12:10.850
Natsuko...

12:17.000 --> 12:20.010
Did I do something wrong?

12:20.550 --> 12:23.310
But all I did was tell Natsuko 
how I feel about her.

12:23.760 --> 12:27.150
Ganger, what am I supposed to do?

12:27.420 --> 12:31.140
Who would've ever imagined 
you'd be asking him for advice on love?

12:31.140 --> 12:32.630
Justice.

12:32.630 --> 12:35.500
I'm sure Ganger'd be so shocked,
he'd spring back to life.

12:35.500 --> 12:36.520
Sh-Shut up...

12:36.800 --> 12:38.530
So what was that about Natsuko?

12:41.740 --> 12:43.030
What?

12:43.030 --> 12:45.660
You've been telling her that
<i>every</i> time you see her?

12:45.660 --> 12:49.020
Well, she doesn't react, so I'm not sure
 I'm getting through to her.

12:49.020 --> 12:50.450
Yeah, she hates you now.

12:50.450 --> 12:51.350
What?

12:52.290 --> 12:53.770
Hey, what's wrong now?

12:53.770 --> 12:56.020
I need to go beg her not to hate me!

12:56.020 --> 12:58.640
Hey now. Just hold up.

12:58.640 --> 13:00.290
Sit your butt back down.

13:02.690 --> 13:08.380
Listen. You're not a little kid, so you can't 
just keep pushing your feelings onto her.

13:08.380 --> 13:10.450
You'll just make her run away.

13:10.750 --> 13:13.060
Then, what am I supposed to do?

13:15.550 --> 13:19.250
When he talked to me about it, 
it was about a friend of a friend...

13:19.250 --> 13:22.940
So why's he being so honest with Justice?

13:22.940 --> 13:25.180
First, ask her out on a date.

13:25.180 --> 13:26.050
A date?

13:26.050 --> 13:30.370
Yup. First, you need to take her 
someplace you two usually don't go.

13:30.370 --> 13:31.730
Someplace we usually don't go?

13:31.730 --> 13:33.810
A cozy restaurant, maybe.

13:33.810 --> 13:37.440
Or a romantic spot at night 
with a great view, you know?

13:37.440 --> 13:41.750
Take her somewhere she's never been
but probably wants to go.

13:41.750 --> 13:43.330
Somewhere she wants to go, huh?

13:43.330 --> 13:46.240
Actually, why didn't you 
just ask Unio about this?

13:45.620 --> 13:46.620
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

13:46.620 --> 13:48.510
There's no way I'd be able to ask Unio.

13:49.390 --> 13:51.370
But you're best friends, aren't you?

13:51.370 --> 13:53.970
We've been together 
ever since we were born.

13:54.420 --> 13:56.270
He's basically family to me.

13:56.550 --> 13:59.540
I've never had a proper family,
so I'm not completely sure,

13:59.540 --> 14:01.900
but I'm pretty sure he's family.

14:01.900 --> 14:05.160
I can't talk to my family 
about my love troubles.

14:05.160 --> 14:07.740
Oh, Luke.

14:08.150 --> 14:11.790
Oh, yeah. I think Natsuko mentioned 
wanting to go to that one place...

14:11.790 --> 14:12.690
Where?

14:14.550 --> 14:16.610
Natsuko, are you here?

14:19.120 --> 14:21.540
Do you want to go to the hot springs?

14:21.540 --> 14:25.140
It's a bit far from here, 
but if you'd like to go...

14:25.620 --> 14:27.060
Why don't we go together?

14:35.520 --> 14:36.940
Hot springs?

14:49.520 --> 14:51.100
Wow.

14:52.400 --> 14:54.300
It really <i>is</i> a hot spring.

14:55.030 --> 14:58.880
Who would've thought there'd be hot springs 
in the world of <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>?

15:05.290 --> 15:08.460
Don't worry. I'll be in the ones over there.

15:18.380 --> 15:19.470
Natsuko!

15:20.060 --> 15:21.970
I just heard a monster!

15:21.970 --> 15:23.150
Are you all right?

15:36.540 --> 15:38.580
I'm surprised there are hot springs here.

15:38.580 --> 15:40.510
Ganger made them.

15:40.510 --> 15:41.200
Oh?

15:41.200 --> 15:44.850
Capitan threw a fit about 
wanting to take a bath,

15:44.850 --> 15:49.200
and Ganger said there'd be hot water here, 
and created them with one punch.

15:49.460 --> 15:53.660
Of course he did. He's Ganger, the "Rock King
 Whose Fiery Magma Flows," after all.

15:53.660 --> 15:55.560
I'm surprised you know about him.

15:55.560 --> 15:59.640
Of course I do. 
I'm a hardcore Nine Soldiers nerd.

15:59.640 --> 16:00.490
Nerd?

16:00.490 --> 16:02.970
It means I really love the Nine Soldiers.

16:04.340 --> 16:05.470
Love...

16:05.830 --> 16:09.110
Wow, so Ganger made these hot springs.

16:11.670 --> 16:13.580
Well done, Ganger!

16:13.580 --> 16:14.900
Admiral Merfolk?

16:14.900 --> 16:15.920
Correct.

16:15.920 --> 16:17.490
You sound just like them.

16:17.490 --> 16:22.120
Right? I used to impersonate them all 
the time. Not that anyone knew who it was.

16:24.960 --> 16:28.270
When the movie first came out, 
they released so much merch for it,

16:28.270 --> 16:30.430
I spent all of my New Year's money on it.

16:30.430 --> 16:35.280
Oh, hey. Who do you think is the 
most popular out of the Nine Soldiers?

16:35.280 --> 16:36.540
Well, me, of course.

16:36.540 --> 16:38.960
Bzzt, wrong. It's actually Unio.

16:38.960 --> 16:41.180
His design is just too strong.

16:41.180 --> 16:44.510
At first glance, he's adorable, 
so I get why he's popular with kids.

16:44.920 --> 16:46.860
Do you also like him, Natsuko?

16:46.860 --> 16:48.960
I mean, I didn't <i>dislike</i> him,

16:48.960 --> 16:52.060
but the one I loved the most 
out of the Nine Soldiers...

16:59.710 --> 17:01.900
<i>"It's you!" Um, yeah.</i>

17:02.380 --> 17:06.720
<i>Am I just imagining that this really
 isn't the time to mention that?</i>

17:08.670 --> 17:09.950
O-Oh, yeah.

17:10.270 --> 17:13.180
So this Kingdom of Reality
you come from... What's it like?

17:13.180 --> 17:13.840
Huh?

17:13.840 --> 17:16.920
I never knew there were more 
than just the nine kingdoms.

17:17.470 --> 17:20.730
I'd love to go to the kingdom 
you're from someday, Natsuko.

17:21.220 --> 17:22.660
<i>That scar.</i>

17:23.340 --> 17:26.310
<i>He's not just some lines 
drawn with a 3B pencil.</i>

17:26.770 --> 17:29.850
<i>To Luke, this world is his reality.</i>

17:30.150 --> 17:33.240
<i>What's going on? My heart's beating so fast.</i>

17:33.610 --> 17:36.490
<i>Must be the heat making me dizzy. 
I should probably get out soon.</i>

17:38.530 --> 17:39.240
Huh?

17:39.240 --> 17:41.080
Uh, Luke?

17:41.520 --> 17:42.500
A Void.

17:42.500 --> 17:43.120
Huh?

17:45.580 --> 17:47.150
In a place like this?

17:47.150 --> 17:48.380
It's heading for the town.

17:48.380 --> 17:49.550
What should we do?

17:49.550 --> 17:51.120
You stay here, Natsuko.

17:51.120 --> 17:52.000
Luke?

17:52.000 --> 17:53.930
It hasn't realized we're here yet.

17:53.930 --> 17:55.960
If it's just one, I can handle it alone.

18:14.140 --> 18:15.280
Luke!

18:15.970 --> 18:16.950
Natsuko!

18:20.040 --> 18:20.780
What?

18:30.270 --> 18:32.000
Natsuko! Are you all right?

18:32.700 --> 18:36.240
Those beams... 
They're similar to the ones I drew.

18:36.240 --> 18:37.100
What?

18:39.090 --> 18:40.380
The hot springs!

18:41.810 --> 18:46.220
You bastard! Those were the hot springs 
where Natsuko and I had our first date!

18:46.220 --> 18:48.150
D-Date? What are you even saying?

18:54.930 --> 18:57.120
That's it, Mister Void.

18:57.120 --> 18:58.440
"Mister Void"?

18:58.440 --> 19:02.490
Bring it on. I'll make you regret
 ever showing up here.

19:02.490 --> 19:05.170
<i>Okay, some kind of switch 
definitely got flipped.</i>

19:06.140 --> 19:07.070
L-Luke!

19:10.130 --> 19:11.370
Crap. This isn't good.

19:11.370 --> 19:13.830
Draw. You need to draw, Natsuko.

19:14.460 --> 19:15.350
Damn it.

19:15.770 --> 19:18.150
Natsuko! I can't get closer 
because of the beams!

19:18.150 --> 19:20.130
Can you give me something to block them?

19:20.330 --> 19:21.910
Block the beams, huh?

19:22.560 --> 19:23.510
That's it.

19:52.400 --> 19:54.330
You get to deal with me!

19:56.630 --> 19:57.430
Are you done?

19:57.430 --> 19:58.670
Almost!

20:01.630 --> 20:03.330
Over here.

20:04.700 --> 20:06.180
Natsuko!

20:08.960 --> 20:11.380
<i>Huh? What is this?</i>

20:14.880 --> 20:17.450
<i>It's like I...</i>

20:24.000 --> 20:25.280
It's done.

20:31.720 --> 20:33.720
Mobile Fighter Ikudas.

20:55.330 --> 20:56.440
That Void...

20:56.660 --> 20:59.950
Just before it lets off a huge beam, 
it stops attacking for a moment.

21:00.130 --> 21:02.600
Natsuko, how is this robot going to move?

21:02.600 --> 21:04.780
It'll walk three more steps, then jump.

21:34.180 --> 21:35.480
It can still fight!

21:47.440 --> 21:48.370
<i>What is this...</i>

21:48.610 --> 21:50.020
<i>I'm feeling right now?</i>

21:50.020 --> 21:51.580
Natsuko Hirose!

21:57.750 --> 22:01.380
I love you!

22:17.740 --> 22:18.960
<i>Squee.</i>

23:50.030 --> 23:54.940
<b>Episode 9: HERO</b>
